      "algorithmDescription": "Computes a pro-rata subscription charge from an annual fee, days used, and a promotional credit. The annual fee is divided by 365 into an intermediate 4-decimal field (PIC 9(3)V9(4)) with ROUNDED, multiplied by days used into a 2-decimal gross charge field (PIC 9(5)V99) with ROUNDED (which truncates any sixth integer digit modulo 100000.00 when the rounded product reaches 100000.00), and reduced by the credit amount with a floor at 0.00.",
      "contract": {
        "inputFields": [
          {
            "name": "ANNUAL-FEE",
            "cobolPicture": "PIC 9(5)V99",
            "description": "Annual subscription fee in dollars and cents"
          },
          {
            "name": "DAYS-USED",
            "cobolPicture": "PIC 9(3)",
            "description": "Number of billable days in the 365-day year"
          },
          {
            "name": "CREDIT-AMT",
            "cobolPicture": "PIC 9(4)V99",
            "description": "Promotional credit subtracted from gross charge, floored at zero"
          }
        ],
        "stdinFormat": "Three newline-separated strings: ANNUAL-FEE (decimal), DAYS-USED (integer), and CREDIT-AMT (decimal).",
        "validInputDomain": "ANNUAL-FEE in [0.00, 99999.99] with at most 2 decimal places; DAYS-USED integer in [0, 365]; CREDIT-AMT in [0.00, 9999.99] with at most 2 decimal places.",
        "outputMeaning": "Single scalar decimal representing FINAL-CHG at scale 2.",
        "outputNormalization": "Trim surrounding whitespace, strip optional leading '+' sign and leading integer zeros (preserving '0' before the decimal point), and format as an exact decimal string with 2 fractional digits (0.00).",
        "semanticAssumptions": [
          "Working-storage intermediate fields: DAILY-RATE PIC 9(3)V9(4), GROSS-CHG PIC 9(5)V99, FINAL-CHG PIC 9(5)V99.",
          "DAILY-RATE has explicit storage scale 4 (PIC 9(3)V9(4)) and is rounded half-up via ROUNDED before being multiplied by DAYS-USED.",
          "GROSS-CHG has explicit storage PIC 9(5)V99 and is rounded half-up via ROUNDED to scale 2, then truncated to 5 integer digits (modulo 100000.00) before comparing against CREDIT-AMT."
        ]
      },
